{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone","id":845732,"title":"Pacts for Everyone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-11T11:09:02-08:00","id":845732,"title":"Pacts for Everyone","content":"Inspiration for this was gained from here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/844027-forcing-open-the-mind-s-eye-developing-supernatural-merits\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...natural-merits</a> Mechanics are shamelessly plucked and stitched together from <b>Demon: The Descent</b>, <b>Summoners</b>, and in part the Changeling 2E spoilers. I tried to keep it so that just about anyone or anything could use these rules, while still leaving the unique deal-making abilities of specific splats relatively unique. Demons are still the only ones who can Pact for Cover, Changelings are still the only ones who can use Sealings, Oaths, and Bargains. Admittedly, there is still overlap, but I tried to reduce it where I could.<br /> <br /> Criticism, suggestions, or comments are always appreciated.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <b>Generic Pacts</b><br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness are a place of mysteries and hidden secrets, wheels within wheels; the supernatural hides behind the ceremony and tradition of cults, fraternities, and subcultures. The supernatural creatures of the world are inclined to keep matters to themselves partially because they would draw attention to themselves if they, but also because it is the unspoken rule of their societies not to involve those who don\u2019t already know what\u2019s going on. Some intrepid mortals, however, can\u2019t resist looking into the dark until their vision adjusts to what they\u2019re seeing. Some mortals seek out arcane power and occult knowledge, building up their abilities through study and their own experience. Others can\u2019t wait that long, and make deals with the numerous things that live in the dark. These are rules for those who need advantages quickly and are willing to pay for them. Supernatural creatures can also enter these pacts with one another, but generally it is mortals who desire the serious boost in power. Most supernatural creatures can take the power for themselves anyways. With Storyteller fiat, mortals with Supernatural Merits can be the one granting power to another. Contracts require a physical vessel that outlines the terms of the deal, but even if the pact is nullified the benefits persist.<br /> <br /> <i>Benefits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Assets:</b> The most common benefit of a pact, and typically the one that those who enter a pact are most interested in, is what you get out of it. These are the temptations people are willing to risk hell for. Generally speaking, Assets are supernatural-to-mortal only, but there have been cases of mortals paying supernatural creatures absurd amounts of money to retain their services. The means by which the Assets are granted vary from supernatural to supernatural- Unchained tweak reality, Awakened can use magic to do the same, Changelings witness pacts to the Wyrd, and Ephemeral Beings can leverage sheer metaphysical might.<br /> <br /> For supernatural creatures bargaining with other supernatural creatures, substitute Merit dots for powers with the appropriate Experience cost if you so desire and if the Storyteller allows it.<ul><li><i>Lesser (1)</i><b>:</b> A one or two dot Merit. Increase a Merit by a dot. A Specialty or a Skill dot. Regain a dot of Willpower or Integrity.</li> <li><i>Medial (2)</i><b>:</b> Three or four dots of Merits. Increase a Merit by two dots. Up to two Skill dots or four Specialties. An Attribute dot.</li> <li><i>Greater (3)</i><b>:</b> Five dots of Merits. Increase a Merit by three dots. Up to two Skill dots and a Specialty. A Power Stat dot (Supernatural Only).</li> </ul><b>Services (Mortal Only):</b> It\u2019s not about what you can do for them; it\u2019s about what <i>they</i> can do for <i>you</i>. When you don\u2019t want power for yourself, either because you fear it or simply because you\u2019d much rather someone else deal with what you want done for sundry and complex reasons. This Benefit stands in for the use of Skill Services (as per page 279 of <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>), Allies, or Retainer keyed specifically to the other named party of the pact.<ul><li><i>Lesser (1)</i><b>:</b> An Availability 2 Service. A favor equivalent to two dots of Allies or Retainer, depending on the nature of the request.</li> <li><i>Medial (2)</i><b>:</b> An Availability 4 Service. A favor equivalent to four dots of Allies or Retainer, depending on the nature of the request.</li> <li><i>Greater (3)</i><b>:</b> An Availability 5 Service. A favor equivalent to five dots of Allies or Retainer, depending on the nature of the request.</li> </ul><b>Sacrifices (Supernatural Only):</b> The proverbial devil\u2019s due, and perhaps the most infamous aspect of pacts. While some supernatural creatures are relatively benign, others are extremely shrewd dealers, working insidious terms into pacts for things the hapless mortal simply can\u2019t resist. The nature of the sacrifice will vary, supernatural to supernatural, and the cost isn\u2019t always worth the prize.<ul><li><i>Lesser (1)</i><b>:</b> A nearly effortless task to performed constantly on behalf of the supernatural creature. Up to two points of Lethal damage or an Availability 1-2 sacrifice. Permitting the Fetter Manifestation to be used on you as a one-time occurrence. Giving up two dots of Merits, a Skill dot, a Willpower dot, an Integrity dot, or a Specialty. This could be as mundane as cutting yourself off from a particular social group, or as esoteric as disfigurement, sacrificing knowledge, or other intangibles. Becoming a one or two dot Retainer/Ally for the supernatural creature. Accept a relatively minor Condition.</li> <li><i>Medial (2)</i><b>:</b> A difficult task that could risk a Breaking Point. Up to four points of Lethal damage, an Availability 3-4 sacrifice, or the ritual sacrifice of an animal. Giving up four dots of Merits, two dots of Skills, four Specialties, an Attribute, two Willpower or Integrity dots. Become a three or four dot Retainer/Ally for the supernatural creature. Permanently become a Fetter for an Ephemeral Being, or permit the one-time use of the Possess Manifestation. Accept a detrimental Condition that will cause you more than a minor inconvenience.</li> <li><i>Greater (3)</i><b>:</b> A task that could risk death and is <i>definitely</i> a Breaking Point. A human sacrifice, an Availability 5 sacrifice. Giving up five dots of Merits, five Specialties, an Attribute, two Willpower dots- alternatively, your Soul. Become a five dot Retainer/Ally for the supernatural creature. Accept the Controlled Condition for an Ephemeral Being. Accept a Persistent Condition that will cause serious issues.</li> </ul><b>Cult (Supernatural Only):</b> A God Am I, say some supernatural creatures. This Benefit is rated between 2 and 5, equaling dots to distribute into appropriate Merits. For a Vampire, this might become a Herd, for a Changeling it might mean Harvest, and for a Mummy obviously it goes to the appropriate Merit. What this means for Ephemeral Beings is up to the Storyteller to decide. The pact signatory becomes the Cult Leader, but if they\u2019re killed the cult goes up in smoke- no Sanctity of Merits. With Storyteller discretion, the cult can come with an appropriate Mystery Cult Initiation, which would then add +3 to the mortal side of the equation. A cult leader must be fully initiated into the cult, after all.<br /> <br /> <i>Terms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Basically, how long you are indebted to the supernatural creature. Most occultists actively seeking pacts only take the Permanent duration- why would you do anything less? However, supernatural beings trying to get their hooks into mortals will often supply temporary, but potent, pacts to lure them into making increasingly steep deals of their own volition. Alternatively, maybe the mortal only needs assistance for a short period of time, or thinks they can make due with a temporary power boost. A pact ends prematurely if the vessel outlining terms is destroyed.<ul><li><i>Day (0)</i><b>:</b> A junkie\u2019s first hit: usually a simply demonstration on the part of the supernatural creature- gratis -to show what they can offer.</li> <li><i>Week (0)</i><b>:</b> Just enough time to get the mortal to rely on what they\u2019ve been given- or accomplish something important.</li> <li><i>Month (0)</i><b>:</b> Lasts a month, exactly. Not the supernatural creature\u2019s fault that some months are longer than others, or that it could end at an inconvenient time.</li> <li><i>Year (2)</i><b>:</b> Great for establishing a longer term hold on a mortal, but without the inconvenience of monthly renegotiation. Fae creatures are fond of adding \u201cand a day\u201d to such durations.</li> <li><i>Permanent (3)</i><b>:</b> Exactly what it says on the tin. If a permanent pact is nullified, the supernatural participant suffers a number of points of Bashing damage equal to their Power Stat. If the supernatural participant is a mortal with Supernatural Merits, they suffer (10-Integrity) points of Bashing damage.</li> </ul><b>Promissory:</b> Pacts <i>normally</i> come into immediate effect, but like any deal, they can come with strings. Promissory delays can be applied to both sides of the pact. A mortal will <i>only</i> give up their soul once something has been accomplished, or the supernatural being will <i>only</i> teach them once several conditions have been fulfilled. This can be useful for the Storyteller if the supernatural being doesn\u2019t have the means to instantaneously grant pact Benefits, because it gives them time to accrue the necessary resources.<ul><li><i>Immediately or At Will (0)</i><b>:</b> The rewards of this side of the pact only come into effect when the signatories touch, or are effective immediately. Common for rewards granted at the cost of \u2018a favor at a later date\u2019.</li> <li><i>Specified Date (1)</i><b>:</b> The Benefits of this side of the pact <i>only</i> come into effect at the specified date and time. If one signatory dies before that time, the pact does not count as broken.</li> <li><i>Conditional (2)</i><b>:</b> The Benefits of the pact are delayed until a specific condition is met. Some supernatural creatures will list several conditions, with the pact considered fulfilled on the success of any one. Each additional condition added past the first adds (1) to that side of the pact.<ul><li><i>Speculative</i><b>:</b> A special form of Conditional pact that relies upon something that the mortal on the receiving end of the pact doesn\u2019t yet possess, like, say, a firstborn, or a business. This adds a point of Willpower to the cost of enacting the pact.</li> </ul></li> </ul><i>Mitigation</i><b>:</b> Pacts can come with incredibly steep prices, and that is functioning as intended, but it still leaves a lot of mortals out in the cold, wondering how they could possibly manage to afford to pay the written cost. Those already privy to the ways of the supernatural, and <i>especially</i> with the pursuit of power, are often formidable negotiators. With Storyteller fiat, supernatural beings with the same advantages could leverage some of these Mitigations against the mortal, usually forcing them to take on Sacrifices.<br /> <br /> <b>Just That Good: </b>Ever heard of the one about the lawyer and the genie? Sometimes, making deals is more than just something that people do as a matter of social interaction; it\u2019s an important part of their lives. Knowing a bad deal when you see one would probably save the lives of hundreds of would-be occultists yearly. Some appropriate supernatural merits can fill in as well.<ul><li><i>Lesser (-1)</i><b>:</b> Fixer, Pusher, Spin Doctor, Sympathetic, Table Turner.<ul><li>Market Sense, Hob Kin, Enchanting Performance (1-2), Gentrified Bearing, Efficient Dealer, Twilight Judge, Lex Magica. Fast-Talker (1-2). Hearing Whispers, Strings of the Heart, Weakest Link.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Medial (-</i>2<i>)</i><b>:</b> Fast Talker (3-4)<ul><li>Enchanting Performance (3), Impartial Mediator.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Greater (-</i>3)<b>:</b> Fast Talker (5)<ul><li>Embodiment of the Firstborn.</li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Initiation:</b> Dealing with the occult to any degree can make you used to quite a bit of weirdness, not least of which is the thought processes of the things that go bump in the night. Access to appropriate information on the supernatural can help as well.<ul><li><i>Lesser (-1)</i><b>:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation (1-2), Covenant Status (1-2), Court Goodwill (3-4), Tribe Status (1-2), Order Status (1-2), Mantle (1-2). A sacred text. Library [Occult] (1-2), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult).</li> <li><i>Medial (-</i>2)<b>:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation (3-4), Covenant Status (3-4), Court Goodwill (5), Tribe Status (3-4), Order Status (3-4), Mantle (3-4). Notes of a true occultist. Library [Occult] (3).</li> <li><i>Greater (-3)</i><b>:</b> Mystery Cult Initiation (5), Covenant Status (5), Tribe Status (5), Order Status (5), Mantle (5). Highly detailed ritual bible.</li> </ul><b>Sanctions:</b> These particular forms of Mitigation are <i>always</i> tied to Conditional Promissory delays, and come into effect if they tried to fulfill the conditions and failed, or become unable to fulfill the conditions. When Sanctions come into play, they last for the rest of the period that the pact would normally run its course unless their effects are immediate or instantaneous.<ul><li><i>Lesser (-1)</i><b>:</b> Lose a point of Willpower, a point of Bashing damage, a -1 penalty to <i>all</i> rolls, a -2 penalty to one Skill, a -3 penalty to a specific roll. The equivalent of a minor Glitch, a mildly inconvenient Condition. Lose equivalent level Benefit.</li> <li><i>Medial (-</i>2<i>)</i><b>:</b> Loss of ability to regain Willpower from rest, a point of Lethal damage, three points of Bashing damage, a -2 penalty to <i>all</i> rolls, a -3 penalty to one Skill, a -5 penalty to a specific roll. The equivalent of a major Glitch, a highly inconvenient Condition. Lose equivalent level Benefit.</li> <li><i>Greater (-</i>3<i>)</i><b>:</b> Loss of ability to spend Willpower, death, Soul Loss, turn Failures into Dramatic Failures, -5 penalty to <i>all</i> rolls. The equivalent of a catastrophic Glitch, a debilitating Condition. Lose equivalent level Benefit.</li> </ul><i>Paying for Pacts</i><b>:</b> Activating a pact costs a point of Willpower on the part of the one who initiated negotiations, plus a point of Willpower for every point of Benefits and Terms one signatory of the pact has over another. If enacting part of the terms of the pact requires the use of a supernatural power, it is used and the required cost paid by the supernatural being in question. Supernatural Fuel Stats may be substituted for Willpower points.<br /> <br /> <i>Using Pacts in the Story</i><b>:</b> The system above is generic and open ended, with the intent of being able to model everything from mortal dealings with Ephemeral Beings, conditions of becoming a Ghoul, becoming a Mage\u2019s apprentice, and anything else you can think of. They\u2019re great for Experience-light games, where a pact grants significant power for the added bonus of an easy addition of drama to the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-13-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:26:59-08:00","id":845772,"title":"","content":"Love it. I think it could be a bit more clear with some examples of how the various parts work, though. And examples are also great for inspiration or story hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:37:40-08:00","id":845779,"title":"","content":"Excellent point- can't go wrong with examples for clarity and as story hooks. This is just a first draft, so I'm obviously going to edit this as I go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:09:39-08:00","id":845799,"title":"","content":"Excellent. You could include something about Loopholes. Those are quintessential to fae deals, but appear elsewhere often. Examples would naturaly include what TV Tropes calls Exact Words. Axelgear wrote a system for <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/836164-buying-your-first-born-pledges-most-dire\"> Rumpelstiltskin Bargains</a></b> that includes loopholes. You could compare notes with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:22:29-08:00","id":845805,"title":"","content":"This looks good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Liking what I'm seeing in this thread, so far. And I'm with GottaGoFeast, there should be a section on Loopholes here. That said, I really wonder how the Binding Vow Numen can be reskinned into a 2E version. It should be something that augments a pact system, at least, not simply give access to it for spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:52:10-08:00","id":845816,"title":"","content":"Loopholes will probably slip in with mitigation. I've got an idea for Binding Vows which I'll probably post here, but it really needs some more tweaking before it's ready for public viewing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:35:04-08:00","id":845875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=845805#post845805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Liking what I'm seeing in this thread, so far. And I'm with GottaGoFeast, there should be a section on Loopholes here. That said, I really wonder how the Binding Vow Numen can be reskinned into a 2E version. It should be something that augments a pact system, at least, not simply give access to it for spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's nothing that stops you from saying that ephemeral beings can make pacts as part of their template. The details would be different for each ephemeral type of course. It's more common to strike bargains with Spirits and Angels, but ghosts and Goetia of higher Rank have their own offers. Free roaming Geister can help you find ghosts who you thought were lost or annihilated, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T17:08:01-08:00","id":845886,"title":"","content":"I love it!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/10p1r2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T01:34:56-08:00","id":845991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=845875#post845875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's nothing that stops you from saying that ephemeral beings can make pacts as part of their template. The details would be different for each ephemeral type of course. It's more common to strike bargains with Spirits and Angels, but ghosts and Goetia of higher Rank have their own offers. Free roaming Geister can help you find ghosts who you thought were lost or annihilated, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>All points I can agree on.<br /> <br /> That said, to tie Binding Vow in with a universal Pact system, perhaps I can rework the idea that the ephemeral entity that applies it to a Pact inflicts a Condition (or several equal to its Rank?) that reinforce its adherence on the spot? Ban, Cursed, and Obsession are all likely choices for such an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T02:03:45-08:00","id":845997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=845816#post845816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loopholes will probably slip in with mitigation. I've got an idea for Binding Vows which I'll probably post here, but it really needs some more tweaking before it's ready for public viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a tentative take for the Numen.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Binding Vow</u></b> <br /> While establishing a pact, the ephemeral entity spends Essence and rolls Power + Finesse. A person unwilling to accept the use of this Numen upon him may reflexively contest it with Resolve + Composure. On a success, the entity may inflict a Ban Condition related to the pact for each point of Essence spent, up to a maximum equal to its Rank. These Conditions last for the duration of the pact, though they may be lifted by supernatural means. Such attempts must roll against the entity's successes, and failure means the pact is treated as broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:15:34-07:00","id":846667,"title":"","content":"Something to fit in the idea of loopholes- a new Mitigation called Clarity. Basically, the supernatural participant in the pact outlines what the pact entails in greater or lesser detail, which can give savvy mortals (and/or PCs) a way to avoid tripping Sanctions and specifically avoiding Conditional factors that would trigger Sacrifices.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity:</b> The traditional pact is one where the mortal is in over their head- they swore a gentleman\u2019s agreement with some strange visitor, and now there\u2019s hell to pay for not following through on it. This does not, necessarily, need to <i>always</i> be true. Some mortals enter into pacts consenting fully, and that honesty can give the Patron some leverage- <i>especially</i> if it gives the Beneficiary a hint towards how to break the pact safely.<ul><li><i>Oblivious (0)</i><b>:</b> The Beneficiary doesn\u2019t understand the Benefits or the Terms of the pact, and it could probably take them a while to understand what happened. In the case of extremely subtle pacts, they might not notice <i>ever</i>.</li> <li><i>Deceptive (0)</i><b>:</b> The Beneficiary understands the Benefits of the pact, but the Terms beyond duration are a little bit shaky. Something about owing them a favor, or \u2018becoming theirs\u2019? Ah well. Best not to think about it.</li> <li><i>Lesser (-1)</i><b>:</b> The Patron specifically goes over what the Beneficiary gets as their Benefits, and the specifics on the Terms. The Beneficiary knows the sacrifices they will make, but not necessarily what that entails. The Patron may use as much poetic language as they like, but it must still allude to, for example, any <i>Sanctions</i> or <i>Conditional</i> <i>Promissory</i> factors.</li> <li><i>Medial (-2)</i><b>:</b> The Patron outlines Benefits and Terms in clear language. Potential loopholes are there if you\u2019re paying attentions, <i>Conditional</i> factors, <i>Sacrifices</i>, and <i>Sanctions</i> are described. The Beneficiary knows the cost of breaking the pact.</li> <li><i>Greater (-3)</i><b>:</b> Cards on the table. Everything, down to the smallest detail, is disclosed. The Beneficiary is capable of truly informed consent to the pact, and the more unscrupulous ones are probably already thinking about how they can get out of the <i>Sacrifices</i> without tripping the <i>Sanctions</i> or breaking the pact.*****</li> </ul><br /> <b>Quick Guide to Pacts</b><br /> <br /> Two Signatories: <b>Beneficiary (Mortal)</b> and <b>Patron (Supernatural)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Step 1. Beneficiary-</b> Apply <b>Benefits:</b> <i>Assets </i>and <i>Services</i>- things the Beneficiary wants from the Patron. <i>Assets</i> last for the <b>Term</b> of the pact, <i>Services</i> are a one-time <b>Benefit.</b><ul><li>Add applicable <b>Mitigation</b>. <i>Just That Good</i> and <i>Initiation</i> apply automatically to the Beneficiary\u2019s <b>Benefits</b>, but the Patron must <u>choose</u> to apply <i>Sanctions</i></li> </ul><br /> <b>Step 2. Patron-</b> Apply <b>Benefits:</b> <i>Assets</i>, <i>Sacrifices</i>, and/or <i>Cult</i>- things the Patron gains from the Beneficiary. <i>Assets</i> and <i>Cult</i> last for the <b>Term</b> of the pact, <i>Sacrifices</i> may be one-time <b>Benefits</b> or reoccur for the <b>Term</b> of the pact.<ul><li>Set the <b>Terms</b> of the pact. The <i>Duration</i> is how long <b>Benefits</b> remain active for both sides of the pact. A <i>Promissory</i> dictates when the <b>Benefits</b> come into effect. Multiple <i>Promissory</i> <b>Terms</b> can be tied to either Patron or Beneficiary <b>Benefits</b>- either as a whole, or with multiple <i>Promissory </i>aspects per <b>Benefit</b>.</li> <li>Add applicable <b>Mitigation</b>. <i>Just That Good</i> and <i>Initiation</i> apply automatically to the Patron\u2019s <b>Benefits</b> or the pact <b>Terms</b>. They must <u>choose</u> to apply <i>Sanctions</i> to <b>Benefits</b> tagged with a <i>Promissory</i>. They must also <u>choose</u> to grant additional <i>Clarity</i> to the pact.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Step 3. Paying- </b>Add up the numbers connected to the <b>Benefits</b> and <b>Terms</b> of both Beneficiary and Patron, and then subtract the <b>Mitigations</b>. The result should be a positive number for both Beneficiary and Patron. If it isn\u2019t, then you should go back and renegotiate both <b>Benefits</b> and <b>Terms</b> until they are. At that point, subtract the lower number from the higher and pay the resulting number in Willpower points, plus one.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> I'll give a few examples per gameline, and I think I'll start with Vampire.<br /> <br /> So, we have Jane the blood doll and she'll be our <b>Beneficiary </b>for today. She's a regular snack for Sheryl the unaligned Daeva, who'll be our <b>Patron</b> and in a post-Kiss swoon Jane begs Sheryl for a taste of what she can do. Sheryl has no intention of making Jane her childe, but she recently learned a Devotion from her sire, &quot;The Wish&quot; (<b>Blood &amp; Smoke </b>pg. 148) and wants to give it a try, and Sheryl has been <i>such</i> a reliable blood doll- how could she say no? Since each Discipline is a 3 or 4-Experience Asset, it counts as a <i>Medial Asset</i>. Jane's part of the pact looks like this:<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Jane)- </b>Celerity 2 (+4), Vigor 2 (+4), Majesty 3 (+6) <b>:</b> Total Benefits (+14)</li> </ul>That is an <i>astonishingly </i>steep amount of Benefits for Sheryl to grant, but it almost certainly will pay itself back. The Devotion already comes packed with a <i>Greater Sacrifice</i>, the <b>Beneficiary </b>gains the Persistent Enthralled Condition which persists indefinitely. Since this only occurs after three nights, let's give it the <i>Permanent Duration</i> with the <i>Specified Date Conditional </i>factor. The <i>Duration </i>of the Benefits is only three nights, so it doesn't add anything to the Terms. Sheryl's part of the pact looks like this:<ul><li><b>Patron (Sheryl)- </b>Benefits Duration [Three Nights] (+0), Greater Sacrifice [Enthralled (Persistent)] (+3) Permanent Duration (+3) Specified Date for Sacrifice [In Three Nights] (+1) <b>: </b>Total Terms (+7)</li> </ul>Since using 'The Wish' costs 5 Vitae, Sheryl just needs an additional +2 to her Terms in order to break even. Since she's so fond of Jane, she decides to add an extra Medial Sacrifice, turning Jane into a 3-dot Retainer for her personal use after three nights. Jane wouldn't mind, after all. Jane loves her. Jane needs her. The symbol of the pact is a business card from Sheryl with her personal cell number and a lipstick-stained kiss on the back. In the end, the pact looks like this.<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Jane)- </b>Celerity 2 (+4), Vigor 2 (+4), Majesty 3 (+6) <b>:</b> Total Benefits (+14)</li> <li><b>Patron (Sheryl)- </b>Benefits Duration [Three Nights] (+0), Greater Sacrifice [Enthralled (Persistent)] (+3) Medial Sacrifice [Retainer 3] (+2) Permanent Duration (+3) Specified Date for Sacrifice [In Three Nights] (+1) <b>: </b>Total Terms (+9)</li> <li><b>Cost- </b>(14-9) + 1 = 6</li> </ul>Sheryl bites into her wrist as Jane waits expectantly, mouth open, on her knees. The Daeva feeds the blood doll five points of Vitae, necessitating an Addiction check and giving her a Stage-One Blood Bond. The process is messy, but Jane is licking up every last drop of the syrupy blood that she can find. Sheryl expends a point of Willpower, and slips the business card into a blood-soaked pocket on Jane's shirt. The blood doll rises as a Ghoul, exultant in her power. In three nights, she'll be Sheryl's, body and soul, and the vampire will have gained a new pawn in the Danse Macabre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T14:13:28-07:00","id":846720,"title":"","content":"From now, I\u00b4m gonna use this hack with Inferno\u00b4s demonologists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:20:13-07:00","id":846739,"title":"","content":"Looking good, so far.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Keep up the good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:54:06-07:00","id":846763,"title":"","content":"Extremely high praise. Thank-you very much! I think I'll model out some Infernal pacts eventually, but in the meantime, let's see another Vampire pact.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> So, it's been a year or so since Sheryl took on Jane as a Ghoul. She's joined the Circle of the Crone, but is clashing with the lead Acolyte of the local cult and has been banned from ever learning Cruac. Fortunately for Sheryl, but <i>un</i>fortunately for everyone else, there's an extremely powerful Strix that's been haunting the city known as Hantu the Sorcerer and she seeks him out for his knowledge of blood sorcery. Hantu, however, is a vicious creature, and his price will not be light. Sheryl wants more than just to learn Cruac, she wants to utterly humiliate the cult leader with her mastery of it, and she isn't really thinking about the consequences right now. Mechanically, this is what Sheryl wants:<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Sheryl)- </b>Cruac 5 (+10) , Initiation [Circle of the Crone] (-1) <b>: </b>Total Benefits (+9)</li> </ul>Hantu is old, Hantu is crafty, but most of all Hantu is wrathful. He hates the Kindred above all else, but he <i>especially </i>despises Mekhet and Blood Sorcerers, and the leader of the local Acolytes happens to be both. The Strix will give her all she desires, for as long as Sheryl shall live, but not without cost. She must Diablerize the Acolyte leader for him. Mechanically, this is what Hantu has on the table:<ul><li><b>Patron (Hantu)- </b>Permanent Duration [Cruac] (+3) , Greater Sacrifice [Diablerize Crone Leader] (+3) , Clarity [Total Honesty] (-3) <b>: </b>Total Terms (+3)</li> </ul>Because of this, the Strix can ask for more- much, much more. Hantu also demands additional sacrifices- a portion of Sheryl's soul to strengthen her Beast to wield Cruac, and the death of Sheryl's Ghoul, Jane, in a horrible, bloody ritual where she must desecrate her flesh and lap the spilled blood from the earth. Because this would also necessitate the loss of Sheryl's Ghoul Retainer Merit, Hantu offers the stone and the earth upon which Jane is sacrificed as an Altar for blood magic, so that she may instruct others in Cruac to further humiliate the Circle, and three dots of the Cruac Style &quot;Opening the Void&quot;. The Pact now looks like this:<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Sheryl)- </b>Cruac 5 (+10) , Initiation [Circle of the Crone] (-1) , Altar (+2) , Opening the Void [3 dots] (+2) <b>: </b>Total Benefits (+13)</li> <li><b>Patron (Hantu)- </b>Permanent Duration [Cruac] (+3) , Greater Sacrifice [Diablerize Crone Leader] (+3) , Greater Sacrifice [Two dots of Humanity] (+3) , Greater Sacrifice [Jane the Ghoul] (+3) , Medial Sacrifice [Ghoul Retainer] (+2) , Clarity [Total Honesty] (-3) <b>: </b>Total Terms (+11)</li> <li><b>Cost: </b>(13-11) + 1 = 3</li> </ul>Sheryl finds the cost horrifying, but she's an outcast in the city and she <i>really </i>wants revenge upon the Circle. With this power, she can do as she pleases and not even the high priestess will be able to stop her. Most pointedly because the high priestess will be dead. Sheryl isn't thinking clearly, and she accepts. A few nights later, she straps Jane to a wide, flat stone with simple ropes, and tears at her flesh with fangs and Vigor-fuelled hands, the weeping wounds forming occult sigils, the blood pooling in a circle around the base of the stone in the shape of the full moon above. She laps at the slowly cooling blood, shedding her clothes, painting symbols across her skin with hands still caked in gore. Hantu perches upon the stone, etching it with his talons, and breaths out a small portion of shadow that Sheryl inhales, eyes rolling back in her head as she performs an ecstatic dance, empowering her Beast to aid her in going and facing the high priestess. When the first creature from the void emerges post-ritual, a thing of blood, smoke, and gleaming yellow eyes, Hantu laughs, eye blazing, as Sheryl runs howling into the night.<br /> <br /> The pact will endure, so long as Jane's desecrated corpse remains intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:30:32-07:00","id":887551,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m trying to create a version of Captain Hook. This one was a detective who traveled to Neverland in order to rescue the children abducted by Pter Pan, a demented Loyalist who regulary perform sacrifices to the Fae with those &quot;friends&quot; who have reached maturity (teenagers) and are no longer fit to play with him, all in exchange of multiple powers: fly ability, living shadow, immortality, plus a whole island as his personal playground.<br /> <br /> Since Hook lacked the power and lifespan to defeat such a powerful enemy, he made a bargain with a local Fae, the Crocodile (heavily based on Tahm Kench of the Leage of Legend). This entity granted him several boons (immortality, dots in dextery and sword style, a ship, etc..). However, The price was high, for Hook refused to sacrificing people\u00b4s lives for his own cause:<br /> Hook would remain immortal as long as he could avoid the Crocodile\u00b4s jaws (for He had marked the formed detective as his prey). Aditionally, Hook must remain in the ship and don\u00b4t leave it for more than a day in the same week. Finally the deal was sealed by offering his left hand to the reptilian Fae as an &quot;appetizer&quot;. The Crocodile doesn\u00b4t expect the former detective to suceed his his quest, and actually enjoys the suffering and desesperation poor Hook suffers in each defeat at the hands of Pan, all while hunting and taunting the increasingly paranoid captain to his inevitable, delectable end.<br /> How can I put this in these rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-11-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:18:04-07:00","id":888106,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. Let's take a look at what Hook is actually asking for, mechanically.<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Hook)- </b>Longevity* (+3), Eternal Youth &amp; Ageless* (+2), Light Weapons Fighting Style (+3), Fighting Finesse [Sword] (+1), Dexterity x2 (+4), Token Ship (+3) <b>:</b> Total Benefits (+16)</li> </ul>And now let's look at the Crocodile.<ul><li><b>Patron (The Crocodile)- </b>Permanent Duration (+3), Conditional Duration [So long as you stay on the ship, and don't leave for more than a day once a week] (+3), Greater Sanction [Remove Longevity] (+3), Medial Sanction [Remove Eternal Youth &amp; Ageless] (+2) Greater Sacrifice [Hook's Hand- Persistent Arm Wrack] (+3), Minor Sacrifice [Cursed- The Crocodile] (+1) : Total Terms (+15)</li> <li><b>Cost: </b>(16-15) + 1 = 2</li> </ul>So, the Crocodile pays two points of Glamour after devouring Hook's hand. The pact will last permanently, but if Hook ever breaks the conditions regarding him staying on the ship, his immortality is simply off the table- he'll start aging again. Notice that this does nothing to his combat abilities, his ship, or his improved Attributes. The Crocodile doesn't actually take a very steep cut, seeing as it expects Hook to fail and for the terms to be violated, and it sneakily ensures it by cursing Hook.<br /> <br /> * These Merits come from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> in the Homebrew Demon Merits thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 05-11-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:45:58-07:00","id":888132,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vhTUQ.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Thank you sir, this was everything I expected <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:35:30-07:00","id":888237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=888106#post888106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea. Let's take a look at what Hook is actually asking for, mechanically.<ul><li><b>Beneficiary (Hook)- </b>Longevity* (+3), Eternal Youth &amp; Ageless* (+2)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, if Hook was fine with staying his current age, he doesn't need Eternal Youth. Longevity + Ageless is enough. Eternal Youth is for those who are already old (or suckers who think it alone means immortality).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=888106#post888106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* These Merits come from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> in the Homebrew Demon Merits thread</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> also copied them to a general CofD Merits thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:07:39-07:00","id":888486,"title":"","content":"I think it should be Ageless (not getting old) + Immortality (nothing can kill him but the Crocodile).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:17:11-07:00","id":888497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=888486#post888486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality (nothing can kill him but the Crocodile).</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that even be priced? The nearest thing I can think of would be to make Hook an Eternal or Abmortal, but both of those have their flaws (and might be beyond the Benefits of the Pact system). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2411\" data-vbnamecard=\"2411\">Raistlin</a> I mean, think about what is being asked for here: <i>nothing</i>, not Aggravated damage, nor nuclear fire, nor the strength of gods can kill Hook other than the Croc?<br /> <br /> Hmm. I can think of a Merit or two that I could whip up that might serve...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T16:57:21-07:00","id":888660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=888237#post888237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> also copied them to a general CofD Merits thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness#post834294\">I did</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:38:06-07:00","id":888851,"title":"","content":"Well in that case it would be the Immortal Dread Power. Most attempts to measure dotless Dread Powers generally puts them at either four or five Experiences. However, it appears as though my math was wrong- Sanctions act as mitigation, they don't add to terms. So the actual total terms is five, meaning that the Crocodile must spend 12 points of Glamour or Willpower. However, the Crocodile could ask for additional sacrifices- the heads of pixies allied to Peter, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:53:26-07:00","id":888861,"title":"","content":"Or maybe Hook must &quot;rescue&quot; a minimum of X children allied to Pan ( turning them into members of his crew) each year. <br /> And maybe each resurrection takes its toll with memories / sanity as the currency, meaning Hook is becoming more and more the insane, cruel pirate Wendy will meet someday . More the irony, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:30:24-07:00","id":889100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=888861#post888861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And maybe each resurrection takes its toll with memories / sanity as the currency, meaning Hook is becoming more and more the insane, cruel pirate Wendy will meet someday . More the irony, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each resurrection paid for with 1 Integrity lost? Hook <i>could</i> keep upping his Integrity to keep up with the costs... but will he? As Integrity falls, the mind becomes more prone to madness and delusions, after all.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Would Inflicting Persistent Conditions (such as specific forms of madness or compulsion, for example) count as Sacrifices?<br /> <hr /><br /> I added some Fated Merits <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness?p=889123#post889123\">here</a> to represent a character being destined for only a specific end, and resistant/immune to any others. Dots for the Advanced and Epic versions are probably in need of change. I was just throwing something out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-12-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:59:06-07:00","id":889210,"title":"","content":"I like the Fated / Cursed approach better. Hook saving his skin every time Just by a tiiiiny margin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-12-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:04:51-07:00","id":889852,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> How well do you think this might apply to other Fairy Tale or Disney Characters?<br /> <br /> Or even as a kind of &quot;cast&quot; spell. By which I mean, the &quot;Patron&quot; crafts a curse/blessing, playing around with +s and -s, and sets the trigger clause that counts as accepting the pact. Like, say, the poison apple in Snow White (balancing Ageless with Persistent Sleep, with the mitigation clause of True Love's Kiss)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:41:07-07:00","id":889882,"title":"","content":"It works extremely well, I'd think. This system was designed to model any sort of deal- mundane, fantastical, mythic, or horrific. You can do Fairy Tale pledges, Faustian bargains, agreements with gods and spirits, corporate mergers, all sorts of things. It's shorthand for Social Maneuvering, legwork to gain supernatural abilities, and flavour for the setting. I tried to make it as user-friendly as possible, so if you can think of a particular bargain between two people, it would probably be able to be modelled by this.<br /> <br /> In regards to 'spells' it is <i>possible</i> but it's not necessarily easy. The <b>Patron </b>could have Sacrifices, Mitigation, and all sorts of things already in mind, but the <b>Beneficiary </b>needs to have something on their end to balance it out and they need to consent to the deal. This doesn't necessarily mean they have to be <i>aware</i>. You could totally have the poison apple in Snow White as the symbol of the pact, the Evil Queen already worked up the entire pact in the poison she dipped the apple in, and Snow White agrees to the pact by biting the apple so &quot;all your wishes can come true.&quot; This isn't, necessarily, on the spot. The <b>Patron </b>already has something in mind when they approach the <b>Beneficiary</b>, so there's a little legwork beforehand, or at least a little thought.<br /> <br /> For Snow White, &quot;True Love's Kiss&quot; wouldn't actually be Mitigation, but a Conditional Duration. The Mitigation would be an unconventional Sanction that ends the Benefits of Ageless and the Sacrifice of Persistent Sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:56:53-07:00","id":889895,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Yeah, I know the <b>Patron</b> would need to think the thing up before-hand. I was just thinking, this models quite well to curses that include hidden (and not so hidden) benefits. The Boons are in there so the whole thing isn't so <i>expensive</i>. Something that could lead to <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CursedWithAwesome\" target=\"_blank\">Cursed With Awesome</a> and such. Due it its &quot;still kind of a Pact&quot;, it still needs the victim/<b>Beneficiary</b> to do something to count as acceptance (eat the gift apple, trespass upon forbidden ground, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:05:54-07:00","id":889902,"title":"","content":"Exactly. They need to do <i>something</i> to consent to it, with or without understanding. Some <b>Patron </b>or other could have the whole thing set up with a Conditional and/or Speculative trigger that the victim/<b>Beneficiary </b>doesn't need to know about, but can still do. All the traditional &quot;unwitting agreement/transgressive act&quot; Tropes are in full effect.<br /> <br /> Reading through Mage 2E, the Acanthus would be <i>particularly </i>proficient at operating like this, especially since a Master of Fate could simply cast Forge Destiny and replicate most, if not all, effects of Pacts. A Disciple of Fate could still wield Sworn Oaths to handle quite a few other aspects. Sacrifices, in this case, could symbolize Yantras contributed by the <b>Beneficiary </b>or a bonus to the roll as 'spell components' as gathered by use of Ritual Savvy Merit enabling the Mage to pump up the Spell Factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:13:35-07:00","id":904302,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> What would be the price for individual powers, such as, say, Contracts? I'm brainstorming a rough framework for normal* (non-template bearing) characters to use the various ritual and minor powers of the various game lines. I had nothing for Changeling, until I thought &quot;maybe a prospective occultist/sorcerer conducts a ritual to make a deal with the Wyrd for temporary access to power&quot;. I was thinking, mechanically, they'd conduct a Pact (as established here) with the Asset as a Contract. They'd still lack Glamour, but Contracts thankfully have a 0 Glamour method of activation (the Catch).<br /> <br /> Seeing as Contracts are priced the same as Merits (1XP per dot), make the Asset cost the same? 1-2 dot Contracts are Lesser, 3-4 are Medial, 5 dot Contracts are Greater?<br /> <hr /><br /> Thought: Could a recurring/repeating transaction be part of a single deal? Such that any time Beneficiary does X, Patron grants Y without having to re-make the same Pact? Mostly I was thinking for the Willpower/Integrity restoration, but made them subject to removal by a conditional Sanction. As long as the Pactee keeps performing their task, the Patron will keep restoring their sanity (Integrity), but if they violate [Obscure Gotcha Clause #237], all those &quot;granted&quot; dots vanish.<br /> <br /> ...Or would this just be Conditional terms N+1? (IE Iteration 1 takes effect when done once, iteration 2 takes effect when done twice, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-31-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:56:20-07:00","id":907395,"title":"","content":"You've got it just right on Contracts. Use the XP value as the means of judging their Asset rating. Forcing them to use just the Catches is certainly an interesting way to produce an atmosphere for the Beneficiary, that's for sure. Alternatively, if you don't want the Pact to bite <i>quite </i>as much, you could give them the Goblin Vow Merit with the Pact, enabling the player to redefine the terms of their agreement whenever it is most convenient.<br /> <br /> In terms of recurring/repeating transactions, I don't see why not. Performing constant tasks is definitely an aspect of a Sacrifice, with the Assets being the restored Willpower/Integrity dot. The Conditional Factor of that Asset would be &quot;whenever they lose a Willpower/Integrity dot&quot; and would translate to N+1. When Terms N+1 run out, and they gain all their Benefits, they are free- they no longer have to perform the perpetual Sacrifice. Making them subject to a Sanction is a good idea, but I would hesitate to make the total value of the Sanctions in terms of just Willpower and Integrity more than a reversal of ten restored dots each, because that would tear the character <i>immediately </i>to the lowest level of Soul Loss and make them pretty close to unplayable. Sanctions are more interesting when they become <i>more </i>than just a loss of power, but when they force other kinds of losses- such as, for example, a quest to make amends.<br /> <br /> It's also worth mentioning that Sanctions are a form of mitigation on the part of the Patron, so they can keep piling on the Sacrifices. A Patron who makes this deal will utterly <i>own </i>the Beneficiary, mind, body, and soul- probably literally. The only way to keep it up is to match the N+1 Benefits with N+1 Sacrifices, which could be perpetual tasks, payments of absurd amounts of money, giving the Patron a house, essentially becoming their slave, etc, etc, etc. Sure, you have an inviolate soul, but that's because it's held in the grasp of a tyrannical god-like creature. Actually... that's a really interesting character idea right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:16:48-07:00","id":907748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=907395#post907395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got it just right on Contracts. Use the XP value as the means of judging their Asset rating. Forcing them to use just the Catches is certainly an interesting way to produce an atmosphere for the Beneficiary, that's for sure. Alternatively, if you don't want the Pact to bite <i>quite </i>as much, you could give them the Goblin Vow Merit with the Pact, enabling the player to redefine the terms of their agreement whenever it is most convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just figured - those Catches seem like nice discounts for Changelings if you happen to meet their conditions. but what would it be like if they were the <i>only</i> way you could apply your magic? Tricking people into fulfilling the conditions, power varying depending upon if you are in your home or not, etc. Really drives home that fairy tale feel. Contacts/Merits are so &quot;cheap&quot; you could easily pile on a number of powers via Pacts without feeling like you are beggaring yourself or selling you soul (leasing it, maybe).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=907395#post907395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of recurring/repeating transactions, I don't see why not. Performing constant tasks is definitely an aspect of a Sacrifice, with the Assets being the restored Willpower/Integrity dot. The Conditional Factor of that Asset would be &quot;whenever they lose a Willpower/Integrity dot&quot; and would translate to N+1. When Terms N+1 run out, and they gain all their Benefits, they are free- they no longer have to perform the perpetual Sacrifice. Making them subject to a Sanction is a good idea, but I would hesitate to make the total value of the Sanctions in terms of just Willpower and Integrity more than a reversal of ten restored dots each, because that would tear the character <i>immediately </i>to the lowest level of Soul Loss and make them pretty close to unplayable. Sanctions are more interesting when they become <i>more </i>than just a loss of power, but when they force other kinds of losses- such as, for example, a quest to make amends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea was more &quot;whenever I do X, I get Y&quot; without having to negotiate a new Pact each time. If your Integrity ever drops, just do X and you get a new &quot;granted&quot; dot, easy-peasy. Or, kill X &quot;monsters&quot; get a new power, all arranged ahead of time. The comment on the Sanctions was, if you violate some stipulation, all those &quot;hard earned&quot; benefits come crashing down. Using a supernatural Pact to prop up your Integrity after engaging in serial murder? Better hope you never kill an &quot;innocent&quot; and violate the Sanction otherwise you are left with your non-Pacted Integrity (likely 0 by now).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=907395#post907395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth mentioning that Sanctions are a form of mitigation on the part of the Patron, so they can keep piling on the Sacrifices. A Patron who makes this deal will utterly <i>own </i>the Beneficiary, mind, body, and soul- probably literally. The only way to keep it up is to match the N+1 Benefits with N+1 Sacrifices, which could be perpetual tasks, payments of absurd amounts of money, giving the Patron a house, essentially becoming their slave, etc, etc, etc. Sure, you have an inviolate soul, but that's because it's held in the grasp of a tyrannical god-like creature. Actually... that's a really interesting character idea right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a rather good character concept...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:29:11-07:00","id":907834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=907395#post907395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also worth mentioning that Sanctions are a form of mitigation on the part of the Patron, so they can keep piling on the Sacrifices. A Patron who makes this deal will utterly <i>own </i>the Beneficiary, mind, body, and soul- probably literally. The only way to keep it up is to match the N+1 Benefits with N+1 Sacrifices, which could be perpetual tasks, payments of absurd amounts of money, giving the Patron a house, essentially becoming their slave, etc, etc, etc. Sure, you have an inviolate soul, but that's because it's held in the grasp of a tyrannical god-like creature. Actually... that's a really interesting character idea right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking in the Emissaries of Power of the Dresdenverse, like the Winter Knight Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:43:47-07:00","id":909192,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of codifying the rules for Hedge Sorcerers (Sorcerer being a gender neutral term here - Hedge Mage, Hedge Witch, etc would also be valid). A couple of ideas:<ul><li>Standardizing or streamlining the method for &quot;summoning&quot; Patrons to get you more powers.</li> <li>Creating mechanical advantages and disadvantages for the sources of your power - &quot;buying&quot; a Contract off a hobgoblin might mean an easier deal, but your source of power is at risk, while contracting with a force of reality or <i>the Wyrd itself</i> (by any name), might net you inviolate power, but cost you dearly.<ul><li>I'm thinking of just automatically granting the higher Powers mitigation in line with the Just That Good reasoning.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> <u><b>Plot/Chronicle Idea(s)</b></u>:<br /> Playing a group of Hedge Sorcerers that are part of some organization. Their oaths to the organization are part of an inherent Pact pre-established with the founder of the organization (Swearing of the Oath and carrying out of duties opts members into the Pact). Maybe model the organization off of Mystery Cult Initiation (granting Goblin Vow at the higher levels)? Or maybe as a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/858523-cults-for-everyone\">Cult</a> with Second Sight and/or Patron?<br /> <br /> Antagonist is a powerful Hedge Sorcerer that has managed to secure a source of Glamor to fuel their abilities (meaning they can just bypass the Catch requirements and use their powers whenever). PCs need to destroy or co-opt their source of power.<br /> <br /> (General Pact based) Antagonist is immortal/invulnerable/powerful through a series of Pacts with various Patrons - they are currently unassailable. The PCs need to track down and eliminate the Antagonist's Patrons (thus ending the Pacts by cutting out the source of power). Kind of like various &quot;kill the sub-bosses before taking on the final boss&quot; games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-08-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:05:14-07:00","id":909244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909192#post909192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of codifying the rules for Hedge Sorcerers (Sorcerer being a gender neutral term here - Hedge Mage, Hedge Witch, etc would also be valid). A couple of ideas:<ul><li>Standardizing or streamlining the method for &quot;summoning&quot; Patrons to get you more powers.</li> <li>Creating mechanical advantages and disadvantages for the sources of your power - &quot;buying&quot; a Contract off a hobgoblin might mean an easier deal, but your source of power is at risk, while contracting with a force of reality or <i>the Wyrd iteself</i> (by any name), might net you inviolate power, but cost you dearly.<ul><li>I'm thinking of just automatically granting the higher Powers mitigation in line with the Just That Good reasoning.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> <u><b>Plot/Chronicle Idea(s)</b></u>:<br /> Playing a group of Hedge Sorcerers that are part of some organization. Their oaths to the organization are part of an inherent Pact pre-established with the founder of the organization (Swearing of the Oath and carrying out of duties opts members into the Pact). Maybe model the organization off of Mystery Cult Initiation (granting Goblin Vow at the higher levels)? Or maybe as a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/858523-cults-for-everyone\">Cult</a> with Second Sight and/or Patron?<br /> <br /> Antagonist is a powerful Hedge Sorcerer that has managed to secure a source of Glamor to fuel their abilities (meaning they can just bypass the Catch requirements and use their powers whenever). PCs need to destroy or co-opt their source of power.<br /> <br /> (General Pact based) Antagonist is immortal/invulnerable/powerful through a series of Pacts with various Patrons - they are currently unassailable. The PCs need to track down and eliminate the Antagonist's Patrons (thus ending the Pacts by cutting out the source of power). Kind of like various &quot;kill the sub-bosses before taking on the final boss&quot; games.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://data.whicdn.com/images/23635156/large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:00:12-07:00","id":909292,"title":"","content":"I was digging through the playtest release for Contracts and saw a number use Wyrd in some of their calculations. So I came up with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness?p=909287#post909287\">this</a> for those cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:03:18-07:00","id":909400,"title":"","content":"The Kings Raven first fanwork was based in something similar, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/MageTheIndebted0.3.5.1.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:36:27-07:00","id":909430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909400#post909400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kings Raven first fanwork was based in something similar, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/MageTheIndebted0.3.5.1.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, deals for power is a common idea/conceit. Though the intent here is to leverage (read: lazily rip off) as much pre-existing material as possible without any (major) changes to the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:37:41-07:00","id":909431,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> How would you go about pricing things like &quot;having a Fuel Stat pool&quot; and the price for Fuel itself?<br /> <br /> Can you make a deal with a Patron to gain a Glamor/Plasm/Pyros pool?<br /> Can you make a deal for Vitae/Mana/Essence itself?<br /> <br /> I could see transactions around Ghouls doing X for Vitae, or Mage's performing deed Y for Mana, but how would that be priced? Lesser for X points, Medial for a full refresh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-07-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:10:56-07:00","id":909811,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> To answer your questions summoning a Patron to make additional Pacts could be modeled with the existing Research and Summoning rules for Ephemeral Beings. Determine a number of successes dependent on relative Supernatural Resistance level (compared to Rank) and how public or private an individual they are. Public reduces the threshold of success, private increases it.<br /> <br /> The potential fragility of Pacts is actually baked in to the system, as each Pact needs a marker and should it be destroyed the Pact is null and void. However, using the Hobgoblin as an example, killing the Hobgoblin without destroying the marker (even if it's an abstract) might not necessarily end the Pact as the Hobgoblin is simply teaching the Contracts, not providing the power for it. Killing a Ghoul's Regnant doesn't remove their knowledge of Disciplines. Destroying an Ephemeral Being providing you with power would probably void the Pact, however. Bargaining with a cosmic being directly means greater power- seeing as you should judge the limits of a certain Patron -and that inherently encourages equal levels of Sacrifices.<br /> <br /> In regards to Supernatural Resistance, there's a Merit in the Hurt Locker spoilers that handles that. It's actually called Supernatural Resistance and is rated from 1-5, granting all the usual effects to the purchaser. It is available to everyone who has at least one dot of Supernatural Merits. If nothing else, your Hedge Sorcerers should get the ability to make more than one Oath. Gaining the ability to store Essence/Mana/Glamour etc would be a Greater Benefit (+3), unless you want to model it with a Merit. Skin Thief has the Essence Pool sub-trait, rated 1-5, and it's a common homebrew Sleepwalker Merit and Wolf-Blooded Tell. A Glamour pool Merit could be drawn up rather easily with similar results.<br /> <br /> Replenishing Essence/Vitae/Mana/Glamour is easy enough. I'd grant it as a one-time Benefit with a number of points equal to the equivalent XP of the rating, and the concurrent Sacrifice being suffering Lethal Damage, performing an equivalent task, or gaining a particular Condition. If you want to improve an existing pool permanently, suffer a Persistent Condition of some kind. Something like that is present in Mage 1e with Mana Investiture Pacts bring made with Acamoth and such. It's easy enough to draw up a Pact basically meaning Deed for Fuel. And in regards to Changeling, I believe Requiem for Regina mentions something named Glamour Fonts that exist where the border between Ironside and Arcadia is thin. I assume they're something like Loci for Faerie, but it doesn't go into greater detail.<br /> <br /> In regards to your organization of Hedge Sorcerers, why don't you post additional ideas in the Cults thread and we can flesh it out there? I'm always happy to test out a system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:35:20-07:00","id":910072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909811#post909811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> To answer your questions summoning a Patron to make additional Pacts could be modeled with the existing Research and Summoning rules for Ephemeral Beings. Determine a number of successes dependent on relative Supernatural Resistance level (compared to Rank) and how public or private an individual they are. Public reduces the threshold of success, private increases it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'll probably use that, mostly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909811#post909811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potential fragility of Pacts is actually baked in to the system, as each Pact needs a marker and should it be destroyed the Pact is null and void. However, using the Hobgoblin as an example, killing the Hobgoblin without destroying the marker (even if it's an abstract) might not necessarily end the Pact as the Hobgoblin is simply teaching the Contracts, not providing the power for it. Killing a Ghoul's Regnant doesn't remove their knowledge of Disciplines. Destroying an Ephemeral Being providing you with power would probably void the Pact, however. Bargaining with a cosmic being directly means greater power- seeing as you should judge the limits of a certain Patron -and that inherently encourages equal levels of Sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would &quot;Pact void upon Patron's death&quot; or otherwise conditional powers be worth Mitigation, or no?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909811#post909811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Supernatural Resistance, there's a Merit in the Hurt Locker spoilers that handles that. It's actually called Supernatural Resistance and is rated from 1-5, granting all the usual effects to the purchaser. It is available to everyone who has at least one dot of Supernatural Merits. If nothing else, your Hedge Sorcerers should get the ability to make more than one Oath. Gaining the ability to store Essence/Mana/Glamour etc would be a Greater Benefit (+3), unless you want to model it with a Merit. Skin Thief has the Essence Pool sub-trait, rated 1-5, and it's a common homebrew Sleepwalker Merit and Wolf-Blooded Tell. A Glamour pool Merit could be drawn up rather easily with similar results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have the exact link for Supernatural Resistance? I didn't think it added to Dice Pools or other calculations for powers. Supernatural Potency is specifically for things like &quot;.. + Blood Potency&quot; in the Dice Pool, or &quot;... lasts Wyrd days&quot; in the effect. It is for <i>not</i>-Supernatural Merits, but rather direct use of main game-line powers (Disciplines, Gifts, Arcana, Contracts, etc.).<br /> <br /> Oh, Hedge Sorcerers in general make plenty of Oaths/Pacts for more power/Contracts. The sample group listed just is party to one bargain that bakes in certain powers. Members are free to expand their power set using an approved list of &quot;vendors&quot;.<br /> <br /> A 1-5 Merit sounds about right. Flat 5 dot/Greater Benefit for simplicity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909811#post909811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Replenishing Essence/Vitae/Mana/Glamour is easy enough. I'd grant it as a one-time Benefit with a number of points equal to the equivalent XP of the rating, and the concurrent Sacrifice being suffering Lethal Damage, performing an equivalent task, or gaining a particular Condition. If you want to improve an existing pool permanently, suffer a Persistent Condition of some kind. Something like that is present in Mage 1e with Mana Investiture Pacts bring made with Acamoth and such. It's easy enough to draw up a Pact basically meaning Deed for Fuel. And in regards to Changeling, I believe Requiem for Regina mentions something named Glamour Fonts that exist where the border between Ironside and Arcadia is thin. I assume they're something like Loci for Faerie, but it doesn't go into greater detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;equivalent XP&quot; so 1-2 points for Lesser, up to 5 points for a Greater? Seems kinda pricey for something so transitory. I was thinking a &quot;full&quot; (or full for non 6+ Power Trait) recharge for something like a Greater Benefit. Or am I undervaluing it? I mean, most supernaturals could acquire it easily enough without deal making, so the main customers would be those with access, but not easy replenishment (such as Ghouls, Alchemists?, Spirit &quot;bribers&quot;, etc.).<br /> <br /> As for Hedge Sorcerers, in the circumstances they'd need/use Glamour, they'd probably trade in Goblin Fruit, or other external sources, mostly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=909811#post909811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to your organization of Hedge Sorcerers, why don't you post additional ideas in the Cults thread and we can flesh it out there? I'm always happy to test out a system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just came up with it in regards to brainstorming Hedge Sorcerers here, and they might just be a Mystery Cult. But sure, I'll post what few ideas I have over there. <hr /><br /> Might Social Maneuvering help with Pacts, or no? Could you &quot;sweet talk&quot; a Patron into giving you a better deal (Mitigation?), possibly linked to Doors opened or something? <hr /><br /> I've got some notes running about turning &quot;active&quot; use of Pacts into its own minor splat. Users would set up a few pre-arranged deals or &quot;spells&quot; that they can invoke in a pinch. As per normal rules for Pacts, they need to establish some condition that their subsequent target(s) &quot;agree&quot; to, however unwittingly.<br /> <br /> A corollary to that was the idea of &quot;Pact&quot; enchanted items. Each is essentially embedded with a Pact that actives upon use. So, for example, a magic sword might grant strength or fighting styles when wielded, provided the user pays its price (in deed, sacrifice, curse, etc.). Or &quot;curse&quot; targets struck with a mix of negative costs combined with odd boons (though I'm a bit more uncertain on this one).<br /> <br /> Ideas on spec-ing out how something like this might work? The item itself would obviously be the Marker for the Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-08-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:32:27-07:00","id":911103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=910072#post910072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would &quot;Pact void upon Patron's death&quot; or otherwise conditional powers be worth Mitigation, or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the example, but I would probably say that counts as Mitigation for the Beneficiary. Exactly how easily killed the Patron is would probably increase the Mitigation factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=910072#post910072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have the exact link for Supernatural Resistance? I didn't think it added to Dice Pools or other calculations for powers. Supernatural Potency is specifically for things like &quot;.. + Blood Potency&quot; in the Dice Pool, or &quot;... lasts Wyrd days&quot; in the effect. It is for <i>not</i>-Supernatural Merits, but rather direct use of main game-line powers (Disciplines, Gifts, Arcana, Contracts, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact text of the Merit taken from the Psychic Vampire template. The end part of it is specific to Psychic Vampires alone, but could apply to other microtemplates with the ability to store Vitae/Essence/Mana/Glamour.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Resistance (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal with at least one Supernatural Merit<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character\u2019s brush with the supernatural left her with an inborn tolerance for the unknown. This Merit acts as a supernatural potency trait for the purpose of resisting supernatural powers. <b>So if a power calls for Blood Potency, Primal Urge, Gnosis, or other traits, use her Merit dots.</b> However, this Merit\u2019s effectiveness is limited by your character\u2019s current Ephemera as well. If she possesses Supernatural Resistance \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, but only has 3 Ephemera at the time, she may only use three Supernatural Resistance dice. (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is explicitly for the resistance aspect of it, but I would rule that it applies for any supernatural abilities they may have gained that require or could benefit from greater Supernatural Resistance. I would include the potentially enhanced senses of Ghouls, improved regeneration for Wolf-Blooded, and an ability to hold more Oaths for Fae-Touched as valid ancillary benefits of the Merit.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=910072#post910072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 1-5 Merit sounds about right. Flat 5 dot/Greater Benefit for simplicity?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably be easiest, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=910072#post910072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;equivalent XP&quot; so 1-2 points for Lesser, up to 5 points for a Greater? Seems kinda pricey for something so transitory. I was thinking a &quot;full&quot; (or full for non 6+ Power Trait) recharge for something like a Greater Benefit. Or am I undervaluing it? I mean, most supernaturals could acquire it easily enough without deal making, so the main customers would be those with access, but not easy replenishment (such as Ghouls, Alchemists?, Spirit &quot;bribers&quot;, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it, it does seem rather pricey. Alternatively, you could have it be a number of points of Fuel for the number of Beats in the equivalent XP. So instead of 1-2 points for Lesser it would be 5-10, instead of 3-4 points for Medial it would 15-20, and instead of 5 points for Greater it would be 15.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=910072#post910072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might Social Maneuvering help with Pacts, or no? Could you &quot;sweet talk&quot; a Patron into giving you a better deal (Mitigation?), possibly linked to Doors opened or something? <hr /><br /> <br /> That is <i>definitely </i>something I would be interested in writing up, but it sounds more like a sub-system of Pacts than something that is integral to their functioning. If I had to throw something quick-and-dirty together, I'd base it off of Impressions more than Doors, as there are only five possible Impressions, while Doors can be positively mountainous. On the other hand, lots of Doors means that the Beneficiary would probably be able to ask for less- with Closed Doors acting towards the total number of Assets. If I was to do that, then the number of Doors would match up to equivalent levels of Benefits. 1-2 Doors would count as a Lesser Benefit, 3-4 Doors would count as a Medial Benefit, 5 Doors would count as a Greater Benefit, and so on.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">[</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">QUOTE=Vent0;n910072]</span></span></span>I've got some notes running about turning &quot;active&quot; use of Pacts into its own minor splat. Users would set up a few pre-arranged deals or &quot;spells&quot; that they can invoke in a pinch. As per normal rules for Pacts, they need to establish some condition that their subsequent target(s) &quot;agree&quot; to, however unwittingly.<br /> <br /> A corollary to that was the idea of &quot;Pact&quot; enchanted items. Each is essentially embedded with a Pact that actives upon use. So, for example, a magic sword might grant strength or fighting styles when wielded, provided the user pays its price (in deed, sacrifice, curse, etc.). Or &quot;curse&quot; targets struck with a mix of negative costs combined with odd boons (though I'm a bit more uncertain on this one).<br /> <br /> Ideas on spec-ing out how something like this might work? The item itself would obviously be the Marker for the Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another really interesting thing. I could see a Merit similar to the Fist of Nightmares from Beast that allows you to have one Pact per Merit that comes pre-made with its own set of &quot;acceptance&quot; conditions. A handshake, verbal agreement, etc. I seem to remember something in the Changeling 1E books that was like 2E's Sealing but nastier in that you could make a full-blown Pledge based on some random, likely hyberbolic, statement a person in your hearing made. That's very fitting for what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Those items are easy enough to draw up. Have the &quot;Pact&quot; be embedded in the object as an 'enchantment' and the agreement to the &quot;Pact&quot; is ownership of the object. You gain benefits, but your life collapses around you as the object's curse takes effect, balancing the scales, or you feel compelled to pursue a certain task, otherwise fulfilling the Sacrifice for the object. If you want to use magical objects as Benefits in a Pact, <b>Flowers of Hell </b>has rules for that on pg. 143 that can be nicely adapted. A one-shot is a Lesser Asset, Knock-offs are Medial Assets, Embedded, Exploited, or Form Gadgets are Greater Assets. If we were to translate this to Mage, then an Artifact, Imbued Item, or Enhanced Item would be worth its Merit dots. Applying it to Werewolf, I imagine a Fetish to be worth its dot rating equivalent (Lesser: 1-2 Medial: 3-4 Greater: 5) with Talens counting as only Lesser Assets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:05:46-07:00","id":913521,"title":"","content":"Thoughts regarding &quot;Pact Items&quot;, specifically weapons. How would either of these two weapons be constructed: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>An Axe that grants great skill to whoever wields it in battle, but it must be fed with blood and/or death, or it turns on the wielder.</li> <li>A sword that bestows death upon those it strikes, but dooms its wielder to loneliness.</li> </ol><br /> I was thinking a &quot;per Combat&quot; Pact for 1, requiring a living Sacrifice (ideally an enemy, but...), with some kind of damaging Sanction if broken. For 2, maybe price its &quot;death attack&quot; as a negative benefit, paid for by requiring a Sacrifice of one of the wielder's Social Merits? <hr /><br /> Another thought (though I'm not sure it should even go here):<br /> <br /> How would &quot;limited use&quot; powers be handled? Like, using Pacts as an example, you make a deal for 5 uses of a Merit, or 7 uses of a supernatural power. It probably shouldn't &quot;cost&quot; the same as unlimited use, but you can't really use any formula for it easily either. Maybe something like Mitigation of 1 or 2, as determined by the Storyteller? So 3 uses of Resources 5 for a Permanent Pact might only count as +1 for Benefits?<br /> <br /> Or is this handled under Conditional Benefits already?<br /> <br /> (My specific desired use for this is an &quot;X uses of Supernatural Tolerance or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness?p=909287#post909287\">Supernatural Potency</a>&quot; Pact, to allow a character to boost their power in a limited fashion. Obviously they'd have to &quot;buy back in&quot; for additional uses.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-14-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:47:48-07:00","id":920541,"title":"","content":"(Golly my first post on a new forum, how exciting!)<br /> <br /> I really love how this system has been set up, and I definitely plan to use it for my next Changeling game to simplify pledges. That being said, I can't help but feel like it's missing a key element to wish-granting in horror, that being contract ambiguity. What if, as an option to mitigate what the bargainee has to do for the bargainer, you could phrase the desired benefits as aspirations rather than specified boons? The benefits would still always fulfill what was promised, but the unfortunate, unforeseen windfalls help balance out the positives (and gives the storyteller a lot of room to have some fun!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11665-a-confused-rabbit","name":"A Confused Rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T14:05:38-07:00","id":920552,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the forums, enjoy your stay!<br /> <br /> To be perfectly clear, much like Pledges in 1e or Pacts in Demon, you don't need to outline every single detail IC. There can still be ambiguity and wordplay, and it is indeed encouraged. However, honesty can be used by the Patron as a way to Mitigate some of their factors and squeeze more out of the Beneficiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T14:52:25-07:00","id":920573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone?p=920552#post920552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome to the forums, enjoy your stay!<br /> <br /> To be perfectly clear, much like Pledges in 1e or Pacts in Demon, you don't need to outline every single detail IC. There can still be ambiguity and wordplay, and it is indeed encouraged. However, honesty can be used by the Patron as a way to Mitigate some of their factors and squeeze more out of the Beneficiary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, for some reason I was under the impression that Benefits couldn't be obfuscated, that makes more sense now. Thanks again for the system!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11665-a-confused-rabbit","name":"A Confused Rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}